//? Title: Iterative Closest Point: Actual Matches, Rigid Updates and Local Failure
//? Subtitle: A planar point-to-point registration study
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given two planar point clouds in different coordinate frames, find a rotation
and translation that align the source with nearby target points without knowing
their correspondence. Independent nearest matches can conflict or collapse onto
one target, making this a local search rather than a pose-recovery guarantee. We
derive the planar rigid update, inspect actual correspondence histories,
preserve the original known-pose example and show an exact local failure.
Returned RMSE now measures the final updated working cloud, correcting the old
pre-update value. Every figure and result is produced by a complete C++ program.
)
\toc

> Start with one point and the error-timing bug

A source point (0,0) and target (3,4) start five units apart. One rigid update
can translate the source to the target; rotation is unidentifiable from one
point, and the zero-covariance computation here chooses zero. The actual history
records pre-update RMSE five and post-update RMSE zero. The former
implementation returned five alongside the new translation, which described
different states. The corrected endpoint error is zero. This is a timing
correction, not evidence that a one-point cloud can identify a unique rigid
pose.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/icp_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto h = dm::geometry::icp_trace({{0, 0}}, {{3, 4}}, 1);
    const auto &s = h.steps.front();
    std::print("| observation | value |\n| --- | ---: |\n| actual selected target index | {} |\n| " "pre-update RMSE | {} |\n| post fixed-match RMSE | {} |\n| post nearest-target RMSE | {} " "|\n| returned final RMSE | {} |\n| translation x | {} |\n| translation y | {} |\n",
               s.target_indices[0], s.pre_rmse, s.post_fixed_rmse,
               s.post_nearest_rmse, h.run.result.rmse,
               h.run.result.translation.x, h.run.result.translation.y);
    dm::geometry::icp_step_diagram(h).save_svg("build/icp_tiny.svg");
}
```
