> A plateau can be the wrong alignment

Take the vertical source (0,−1),(0,1) and horizontal target (−1,0),(1,0). Both
initial computed distances tie, so both source points choose target zero. The
centered matched target is zero, leaving zero covariance. The first update
translates the source left by one and keeps angle zero. Its error is one; the
same correspondences then repeat. Yet a quarter turn maps the original source
onto both target points and has near-zero numerical error. ICP's actual stop
therefore fails to recover an available exact rigid alignment.

The stop is specifically a strict absolute change between consecutive PRE-update
RMSE values, tested after applying an update. Retaining that legacy rule
preserves ordinary finite-input poses and update counts. It does not test the
fixed-match minimizer's uniqueness or the parameter step. Zero tolerance forces
the requested budget even at an unchanged cloud; the first pre-error has no
earlier finite comparison. `PreUpdatePlateau`, `IterationLimit` and `EmptyCloud`
name those different outcomes without a convergence guarantee.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/icp_local.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> source{{0, -1}, {0, 1}}, target{
        {-1, 0}, {1, 0}
    };
    const auto h = dm::geometry::icp_trace(source, target, 10, 1e-14);
    const auto quarter =
        dm::geometry::icp_transform_points(source, std::acos(-1.) / 2);
    const auto candidate = dm::geometry::icp_run(quarter, target, 0);
    std::print("| control | observed |\n| --- | ---: |\n| initial target indices | {} {} |\n| returned " "angle | {} |\n| returned shift x | {} |\n| plateau updates | {} |\n| returned final RMSE | " "{} |\n| explicit quarter-turn RMSE | {:.12g} |\n",
               h.steps.front().target_indices[0],
               h.steps.front().target_indices[1], h.run.result.angle,
               h.run.result.translation.x, h.run.result.iterations,
               h.run.result.rmse, candidate.result.rmse);
    if (h.run.stop != dm::geometry::IcpStop::PreUpdatePlateau ||
        h.run.result.rmse != 1)
        throw std::runtime_error("local plateau control");
    auto p = dm::geometry::icp_alignment_plot(source, target, h.run);
    p.title("Wrong plateau: a quarter-turn solution exists").x_limits(-2, 2).y_limits(-2, 2).save_svg("build/icp_local.svg");
}
```
