\alttext(Vertical source translates left, both points remain above and below target zero, and the unused target at plus one exposes the many-to-one failure.)

> Work and complete admission policies

For K updates, N source points and M targets, the brute-force producing nearest
search evaluates K·N·M squared distances, while K·N working-point updates are
counted separately. Centroids, covariance, trigonometry, validation,
comparisons, copies and allocations are outside these selected counts. Ordinary
execution adds one N·M final-error observation. Capture adds N fixed-match plus
N·M fresh nearest distances after every update; those are explicitly diagnostic
work. There is no repeated-prefix solve used to manufacture a history.

Input must have finite coordinates, finite nonnegative tolerance and a
nonnegative integer budget. Complete validation precedes input/working copies. A
finite input can overflow subtraction, squared distances, sums, covariance or
pose updates; checked arithmetic throws, without automatic rescaling. Small
quantities can underflow or lose precision. Empty inputs keep the legacy
identity/zero-RMSE convention, which says nothing about fit; zero budget on two
nonempty clouds instead reports the real initial directed error.

New run/trace policies default to one million combined source-plus-target points
and one million logical history entries. Zero disables either optional cap. Each
captured step costs 1+5N units: one record, two coordinates per before point,
one chosen index and two coordinates per after point. The complete step is
admitted before its producing nearest pass, copies or update. Excluded are input
copies, ordinary/transient arrays, final output cloud/result/work, scalar
metadata, capacity and byte/peak RAM. Untraced execution ignores the history
cap; the legacy `icp` entry point disables both optional caps. Exceptions return
no partial trace. All returned clouds and records own their values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/icp_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto source = dm::geometry::icp_example_source();
    const auto target =
        dm::geometry::icp_transform_points(source, .12, {.7, -.5});
    std::vector<double> budgets, producing, observed;
    std::print("| forced updates | producing distances | trace diagnostic distances | point updates | " "logical step entries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int k : {1, 2, 4, 8, 16}) {
        const auto h = dm::geometry::icp_trace(source, target, k, 0);
        const auto &w = h.run.work;
        if (w.distance_evaluations != std::size_t(k) * 625 ||
            w.diagnostic_distance_evaluations != std::size_t(k) * 650 ||
            w.point_updates != std::size_t(k) * 25)
            throw std::runtime_error("work identity");
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", k, w.distance_evaluations,
                   w.diagnostic_distance_evaluations, w.point_updates,
                   h.steps.size() * 126);
        budgets.push_back(k);
        producing.push_back(w.distance_evaluations);
        observed.push_back(w.diagnostic_distance_evaluations);
    }
    const auto tiny =
        dm::geometry::icp_trace({{0, 0}}, {{1, 0}}, 2, 0, {2, 12});
    try {
        (void) dm::geometry::icp_trace({{0, 0}}, {{1, 0}}, 2, 0, {2, 11});
        throw std::runtime_error("cap accepted");
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        std::print("Two one-point steps admit 12 logical units; cap 11 is rejected.\n");
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(budgets, producing, "producing", {37, 99, 235}, 2).line(
        budgets, observed, "diagnostic", {220, 38, 38}, 2).title(
        "Trace observations are additional work").x_label(
        "forced actual updates").y_label("squared-distance evaluations").y_limits(0, 12500).save_svg("build/icp_work.svg");
}
```
